Taking a thread's process takes it off its queue but leaves it in the state it had,
so a woken or resumed one runs in a process that is gone;
a thread without a process is stopped.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: thread without a process is not stopped

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -276,7 +276,6 @@ void sched_unhost(struct cap *hosted)
     if (t->state == THREAD_WAITING) {
         unwait(t);
     }
-    t->state = THREAD_STOPPED;
     *hosted = (struct cap){ 0 };
     thread_settle(t);
 }
